  "generated_text": "1. Consider the expression \\((x+y+z)^{2006} + (x-y-z)^{2006}\\).\n2. Expand each term using the binomial theorem.\n3. The binomial theorem states that \\((a+b+c)^n\\) and \\((a-b-c)^n\\) are symmetric polynomials in \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\).\n4. When expanded, each term in the expansion will have the same degree and coefficients of \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\).\n5. Therefore, the number of terms in the expanded form of each polynomial is \\(2007\\) (since each term in the expansion of \\((a+b+c)^n\\) and \\((a-b-c)^n\\) has \\(n+1\\) terms).\n6. Since there are two such terms, the total number of terms in the expanded expression is \\(2007 + 2007 = 4014\\).\n\nThus, the number of terms in the simplified expression of \\((x+y+z)^{2006} + (x-y-z)^{2006}\\) is \\(\\boxed{4014}\\).",
  "grade": {
